#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Read the resource usage {#read-the-resource-usage}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The result metadata reports `CPU_TIME` for phases other than `RUNNING: "
"EXECUTING_QPU`, when it is available. The `RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU` phase can"
" report `QPU_TIME`, the QPU usage returned by Quantum Compute, if the final "
"usage is available for every Quantum Compute job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, you downloaded an MIS instance from QOBLIB, formulated it "
"as a QUBO with `qiskit-addon-opt-mapper`, connected to SQOA Solver, "
"configured and submitted the workload, mapped the returned assignment back "
"to the graph, and checked the selected nodes against the original graph.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You also compared the result with the QOBLIB reference solution, examined "
"the contribution of the classical post-processing, and inspected the "
"resource usage of each execution phase.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SQOA Solver combines presolve, QRAO with a QRAC-based encoding, sampling-"
"circuit construction, hardware-aware transpilation, sample-based "
"diagonalization, rounding, and classical refinement. This workflow can map "
"more binary variables than a one-variable-per-qubit encoding would allow. "
"The amount of reduction from presolve and encoding depends on the problem "
"structure, and solution quality depends on the samples obtained.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `shots` and `postprocessing_level` settings control the quantum sampling"
" budget and the classical refinement, respectively, without changing the "
"submission workflow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Appendix: Submit the problem as an OMMX instance {#appendix-submit-the-"
"problem-as-an-ommx-instance}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SQOA Solver also accepts an `ommx.v1.Instance` from the [OMMX](https://jij-"
"inc.github.io/ommx/en/introduction.html) SDK. The [OMMX Quantum "
"Benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/) package "
"distributes the QOBLIB problems as OMMX instances together with their "
"reference solutions, so you can load the same QUBO without formulating it "
"yourself.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With an OMMX input, `objective_value` is evaluated in the sense of the "
"instance, and the result also contains the canonical `ommx.v1.Solution`. "
"Install the package, which also installs the OMMX SDK:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Load the `binary_unconstrained` model of the same instance. The dataset "
"loader prints progress messages, so the code captures them to keep the "
"output compact.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SQOA Solver receives an OMMX instance as a standard padded Base64 string and"
" returns the canonical solution in the same format. Define two helper "
"functions for this conversion:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`to_problem_payload()` serializes an `ommx.v1.Instance` into the string that"
" you pass as `problem`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`to_ommx_solution()` decodes the canonical `ommx.v1.Solution` from the "
"result.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Submit the instance with the same inputs as before, replacing only "
"`problem`. Then decode the canonical solution and read the selected nodes by"
" variable name.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"* Apply the workflow to your own QUBO problems. Build an `OptimizationProblem` as shown in the [SQOA Solver guide](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver). The steps for conversion and submission remain the same, but adapt the validation to the structure of your problem.\n"
"* Submit the problem as an OMMX instance, as shown in the [appendix](#appendix-submit-the-problem-as-an-ommx-instance). See the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/jij-sqoa-solver) for the accepted problem formats and the returned fields.\n"
"* Explore other independent-set instances in the [QOBLIB repository](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset) or through [OMMX Quantum Benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/).\n"
"* Learn more about modeling with [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper/) or [JijModeling](https://jij-inc-jijmodeling-tutorials-en.readthedocs-hosted.com/en/latest/introduction.html) and exchanging problems with [OMMX](https://ommx-en-book.readthedocs.io/en/latest/).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

